  "topic_en": "Expressing points p^3, p^4, ... of a polygon/pentagon configuration as linear combinations of p^1 and p^2, deriving general formulas for the coefficients m^k, n^k in terms of a, b, c, d, and evaluating them numerically for the regular pentagon.",
  "transcription": "Erste Art {+Math. 26+} von $p^0$ angezählt. (1) [-47.1-] 1\nIn einer geraden liegen\n$p^1$\n$p^2$\n$p^3 = ap^1 + bp^2$\n$p^4 = cp^1 + dp^2$\n$p^5 = m^5p^1 + n^5p^2$\n$p^6 = m^6p^1 + n^6p^2$\n$p^7 = m^7p^1 + n^7p^2$\nu.s.w\n2.4.5.6\n[-0.3.6.7-]\n[-1.4.7.8-]\n0 2 8 9\n1 3 5 9\nDreiecke\n$a = \\frac{y^2x^3 - x^2y^3}{x^1y^2 - y^1x^2}$ oder\n$b = \\frac{x^1y^3 - y^1x^3}{x^1y^2 - y^1x^2}$\nFür das ordentliche Pentagon\n$a = -1,618034$\n$b = +1,618034$\n$c = -1,618034$\n$d = +1$\n$m^5 = \\frac{c(a+b-1)}{bc-(a-1)(d-1)}$\n$n^5 = \\frac{b(c+d-1)}{bc-(a-1)(d-1)}$\n$m^6 = \\frac{ac}{c+bc-ad}$\n$n^6 = \\frac{bc}{c+bc-ad}$\n$m^7 = \\frac{ad}{b+ad-bc}$\n$n^7 = \\frac{bd}{b+ad-bc}$\n$m^8 = 0$\n$n^8 = \\frac{d}{1-c}$\n$m^9 = 0$\n$n^9 = \\frac{b}{1-a}$\n$m^5 = -0,618$\n$n^5 = +1$\n$m^6 = -1$\n$n^6 = +1$\n$m^7 - 0.618$\n$n^7 = +0,618$\n$m^8 = 0$\n$n^8 = +0,382$\n$m^9 = 0$\n$n^9 = +0,618$",
